          "N is zoned decimal, one byte per digit; P is packed decimal, (digits ÷ 2) + 1 bytes with the sign in the last nibble.",
          "D is a Natural date and T a Natural time, stored packed (4 and 7 bytes); B, I, F and L take their stated length in bytes.",
